        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A treadmill works the quadriceps, hamstrings, glutes, calves and
            hip flexors, but it is cardiovascular exercise first.</strong> Walking, running,
            incline and walking backwards shift the emphasis between those muscles, while the
            biggest training effect lands on the heart and lungs, with leg endurance rather than
            strength or size.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Use it for cardio, let go of the rails so the legs do the work, build speed and grade
            gradually, and add strength training for the upper body and for real leg strength. For
            the wider case for the machine, see our guide to the
            <a href="/benefits-of-treadmill-exercise/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">benefits of treadmill exercise</a>.
          </p>
